# Value Steward mk II — daily cron template.
#
# NOT installed anywhere by checking this file in. Customize the paths below,
# then install with `crontab crontab` (or merge into an existing crontab).
#
# One job, run_daily, in a retry window rather than at one precise instant.
# The rule reads a finalized daily close, which is not published exactly at
# market close, and close time itself varies (1pm ET on early-close days,
# per the exchange calendar in market_calendar.py) -- so the window opens
# comfortably after the LATEST normal close (4pm ET) and checks every 15
# minutes for 90 minutes, covering an early-close day's bar (published hours
# earlier) just as well as a normal day's. run_daily.py's own once-per-day
# guard (see last_logged_day in decision_log.py) makes every attempt after
# the first a harmless no-op, so widening this window costs nothing --
# exactly the wide-retry-window-plus-idempotent-guard pattern
# value-steward's own EOD cron used, reused rather than reinvented.
#
# Local system clock is assumed to read US Eastern time directly, matching
# value-steward's own crontab convention there -- confirm this holds before
# installing; if the machine's clock is UTC or something else, convert.
#
# DRY RUN BY DEFAULT. This line does not place any order -- it computes and
# logs today's decisions only. Add --execute (a second, separate, deliberate
# line below) only once you have decided to let it trade unattended.
15,30,45 16 * * 1-5 cd /home/YOUR_USER/value-steward-2 && /home/YOUR_USER/value-steward-2/.venv/bin/python -m vs2.run_daily >> /home/YOUR_USER/value-steward-2/logs/run_daily.log 2>&1
0,15,30,45 17 * * 1-5 cd /home/YOUR_USER/value-steward-2 && /home/YOUR_USER/value-steward-2/.venv/bin/python -m vs2.run_daily >> /home/YOUR_USER/value-steward-2/logs/run_daily.log 2>&1

# To let it actually place orders once armed, replace both lines above with
# the same two lines plus `--execute`:
#
# 15,30,45 16 * * 1-5 cd /home/YOUR_USER/value-steward-2 && /home/YOUR_USER/value-steward-2/.venv/bin/python -m vs2.run_daily --execute >> /home/YOUR_USER/value-steward-2/logs/run_daily.log 2>&1
# 0,15,30,45 17 * * 1-5 cd /home/YOUR_USER/value-steward-2 && /home/YOUR_USER/value-steward-2/.venv/bin/python -m vs2.run_daily --execute >> /home/YOUR_USER/value-steward-2/logs/run_daily.log 2>&1
